<!--
    File: prop_apc_13x8.xml
    Author: Cheon
    APC 13x8 fixed-pitch propeller, static-bench calibration.

    Geometry:
      Diameter: 13 in = 0.3302 m.
      Geometric pitch: 8 in/revolution = 0.2032 m/revolution.
      Pitch/diameter: 8/13 = 0.615384615.
      Two blades and direct drive are retained assumptions; verify the hardware.
      JSBSim minpitch/maxpitch are blade angles in degrees, NOT pitch in inches.
      The representative angle at 75% radius is atan(8/(0.75*pi*13)) = 14.637383 deg.
      Equal minpitch/maxpitch selects the fixed-pitch, one-dimensional J tables.

    Source: user-supplied APC 13x8 static bench screenshot.
    Transcribed inputs: prop_apc_13x8_static.csv (same directory).
    Units assumed from the bench sheet: thrust in gram-force, torque in N*m,
    voltage in V, current in A, electrical power in W. PWM is in microseconds.
    The motor/ESC configuration must match this experiment when reproducing PWM/RPM.

    PWM 1100 handling:
      The sheet reports RPM=0 with 39.44 gf thrust and 0.0089 N*m torque.
      Per the operator, RPM was likely below the tachometer measurement range.
      CSV RPM is therefore EMPTY (unavailable), not a stopped-propeller sample.
      Exclude this row from ALL RPM-based fits. Its derived zero shaft power,
      zero efficiency and division-by-zero thrust coefficient are not measurements
      of valid zero-output operation. No replacement RPM is fabricated.

    Static calibration, using all nine measured-RPM rows (PWM 1200 to 1900):
      Assumed air density rho = 1.225 kg/m^3; ambient density was not supplied.
      g = 9.80665 m/s^2, D = 0.3302 m, n = RPM/60 revolutions/s.
      T = thrust_gf * g/1000 [N].
      P_shaft = torque_nm * 2*pi*n [W], NOT the electrical input power.
      CT = T/(rho*n^2*D^4), CP = P_shaft/(rho*n^3*D^5).
      Fit T against n^2 and P_shaft against n^3 independently through the origin:
        CT(0) = sum(n^2*T) / (rho*D^4*sum(n^4)) = 0.079725849.
        CP(0) = sum(n^3*P_shaft) / (rho*D^5*sum(n^6)) = 0.040192093.
      The sheet's coefficient/RPS/efficiency columns are not fitting inputs;
      coefficients are recomputed from the measured RPM, thrust and torque.
      A single static coefficient cannot reproduce RPM-dependent scatter exactly:
      thrust RMSE is about 65.27 gf, max relative error about 9.42% over fitted rows.
      Recalibrate if actual bench density or measurement units differ.

    Highest measured point (not a certified maximum rating or a 100% PWM point):
      PWM 1900, 8774.90 RPM, 2544.13 gf, 0.6728 N*m, 22.43 V, 32.47 A,
      728.61 W electrical input; recomputed shaft power approximately 618.24 W.
      Model at this RPM and rho: approximately 2532.24 gf and 604.55 W shaft power.
      The folder name goshawk_10s does not mean these are 10S-voltage measurements.
      This experiment spans 22.43 to 23.79 V; do not extrapolate to 10S unvalidated.

    Advance-ratio tables:
      J = V/(n*D). Only J=0 is bench-calibrated.
      J>0 is a PROVISIONAL estimate, not measured forward-flight performance.
      Reuse the normalized shape of prop_apc_12x6.xml, with J stretched by
      (8/13)/(6/12) = 16/13, and coefficients scaled to the fitted static values:
        J_new = J_12x6 * 16/13.
        CT_new = CT_12x6 / 0.09292 * CT(0).
        CP_new = CP_12x6 / 0.04067 * CP(0).
      This pitch-ratio scaling is only a placeholder. Windmilling, negative J,
      cruise efficiency, and operation outside the measured RPM range are unverified.

    Propeller-only model: PWM-to-RPM, ESC behavior, motor losses and voltage sag
    are not calibrated here. APC 13x8 is confirmed hardware and this file is
    selected by all four thrusters in propulsion_goshawk_10s.xml.
-->
<propeller name="prop_apc_13x8">
    <!-- Unmeasured inertia: retain the previous 12x6 placeholder until mass/inertia
         is measured. This value is NOT a calibrated 13x8 transient response. -->
    <ixx unit="SLUG*FT2"> 0.0002 </ixx>
    <diameter unit="IN"> 13 </diameter>
    <numblades> 2 </numblades>
    <gearratio> 1.0 </gearratio>

    <!-- Fixed blade angle in degrees at 75% radius; geometric pitch is 8 inches. -->
    <minpitch> 14.637383 </minpitch>
    <maxpitch> 14.637383 </maxpitch>
    <minrpm> 0 </minrpm>
    <!-- Measured upper reference only: maxrpm is a governor setting, not a hard
         RPM clamp for this fixed-pitch model. No constant-speed governor. -->
    <maxrpm> 8774.90 </maxrpm>
    <constspeed> 0 </constspeed>

